  "metadata": {
    "title": "The vertex centroid of focal antipedals of even elliptic billiards",
    "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23220043",
    "publication_date": "2026-10-07",
    "description": "<p>We prove invariant k405 for the original-polygon, full-line antipedals of elliptic billiards with a strictly nested nondegenerate confocal elliptical caustic and even least period. The unweighted vertex centroid is zero for the center pole and has an explicit phase-independent focal coefficient determined by the axes, caustic parameter, period and perimeter. The proof covers primitive star polygons and either orientation; the circle is treated separately. Repeated odd polygons with even list length and hyperbolic or degenerate caustics are outside the theorem. A self-contained finite-action and perimeter-stationarity proof and portable exact verification supplement are supplied.</p><p>This answers k405 as posed without proof in Reznik-Garcia-Koiller's 2020/2021 source. Ferudun's later deposited note, DOI 10.5281/zenodo.23092466, states the same theorem and coefficient and uses the same pair-and-moment mechanism; that overlap is explicitly credited. A proof was publicly posted in PR140 on September 30, 2026, before the specific overlapping Zenodo record was created on October 1. The bounded primary-source audit did not establish an earlier complete answer. No absolute priority, exclusive theorem novelty, independent-discovery, copying or collaboration claim is made. The problem is not described as still unsolved at this note's publication.</p><p>AI tools were used extensively in developing, drafting, reproducing and adversarially auditing this work. Independent AI reviews are not conventional human peer review. This preprint is unrefereed and has not undergone conventional human peer review.</p>",
